mmm, good point.  Again, I'm really not sure about this so please, anyone
with more experience jump in if I have this wrong but the way I see it is as
follows:

du creates the closest relationship in saying that these two labels refer to
the same actual object

mintu is next in that it says that the two objects are "interchangeable" so
they are identical in every conceivable way but are still two distinct
objects.

dunli means that the two objects are congruent/equal to but since it gives
the x3 position to specify in what property they are equal I understand
dunli to mean that they are equal in some way, not necissarily in EVERY way.

long story short:  IMO du makes labels refer to same object.  mintu makes
distinct objects identical.  dunli makes two distinct objects equal in some
property x3

- Luke Bergen


